    ('EIFFELTOWER', 'Iron Lattice Spire', 'Wrought-iron lattice tower on the Champ de Mars in Paris named after Gustave Eiffel.', "Constructed as the entrance arch for the 1889 World's Fair; stands 1,083 feet tall."),
    ('EINSTEIN', 'Relativity Genius', 'German-born theoretical physicist who developed the theories of special and general relativity.', 'Won the 1921 Nobel Prize for explaining the photoelectric effect; formula E=mc².'),
    ('ELEMENT', 'Pure Chemical Substance', 'Pure substance consisting entirely of atoms that all have the identical atomic number.', 'Organized systematically on the Periodic Table created by Dmitri Mendeleev in 1869.'),
    ('ELM', 'Deciduous Tree', 'Tall shade tree with serrated leaves historically lining urban boulevards.', 'Known for graceful arching canopies over classic European streets.'),
    ('EMPIRE', 'Domain of Nations', 'Extensive group of states or countries under a single supreme authority.', 'The British Empire, Roman Empire, and Ottoman Empire spanned continents.'),
    ('ENERGY', 'Work Capacity', 'Quantitative property that must be transferred to an object to perform work.', 'Exists in kinetic, potential, thermal, chemical, and nuclear forms.'),
    ('ENLIGHTENMENT', 'Age of Reason', 'European intellectual movement in the 17th and 18th centuries emphasizing reason.', 'Promoted religious tolerance, scientific inquiry, individual liberty, and democracy.'),
    ('ENZYME', 'Protein Catalyst', 'Biological protein molecule that accelerates biochemical reactions in cells.', 'Lowers activation energy, enabling rapid metabolic digestion of food.'),
    ('EPIC', 'Grand Odyssey', 'Lengthy narrative poem recounting grand heroic deeds and adventures.', 'Famous examples include Gilgamesh, the Iliad, and the Odyssey.'),
    ('EQUATORIAL', 'Equator Zone', "Relating to the tropical regions situated immediately along the Earth's equator.", 'Characterized by warm temperatures, dense rainforests, and heavy annual rains.'),
    ('EQUINOX', 'Equal Day and Night', "Time of year when the Sun passes directly over Earth's equator, making day and night equal length.", 'Occurs twice annually around March 20 (vernal equinox) and September 23 (autumnal equinox).'),
    ('ESTUARY', 'Tidal River Mouth', 'Partially enclosed coastal body of water where fresh river water mixes with salty sea.', 'Serves as a productive marine nursery sheltering juvenile fish, crabs, and wading birds.'),
    ('ETNA', 'Sicilian Volcano', 'The highest active volcano in Europe, rising continuously on the island of Sicily.', 'In Greek mythology, the deadly monster Typhon was trapped beneath Mount Etna by Zeus.'),
    ('EURO', 'European Single Currency', 'Official currency of the Eurozone member states within the European Union.', 'Represented by the euro symbol (€) and managed by the European Central Bank.'),
    ('EUROPA', 'Ocean Moon', 'Smooth, ice-crusted moon of Jupiter harboring a vast global liquid saltwater ocean beneath.', 'Heated by tidal flexing; regarded by astrobiologists as a prime candidate for life.'),
    ('EVEREST', 'Roof of the World', 'The highest mountain above sea level on Earth, rising 29,031 feet in the Himalayas.', 'Located on the border of Nepal and China; known as Sagarmatha and Chomolungma.'),
    ('EXOPLANET', 'Extrasolar World', 'Planet located outside our solar system orbiting another distant star.', 'Discovered by transit dips using space telescopes like Kepler and James Webb.'),
    ('EYE', 'Visual Organ', 'Sensory organ focusing light onto retinas to provide visual sight.', 'Features a cornea, pupil, adjustable lens, and retinal receptors.'),
    ('FJORD', 'Glacial Sea Inlet', 'Long, deep, narrow sea inlet with steep cliffs created by ancient glacial erosion.', 'World-famous in Norway, New Zealand, and Alaska for breathtaking sheer rock waterfalls.'),
    ('FLUTE', 'Woodwind Aerophone', 'Woodwind instrument that produces sound from the flow of air across an embossed mouth hole.', 'One of the earliest musical instruments known; made of metal, wood, or bamboo.'),
    ('FOG', 'Ground Cloud', 'Thick cloud of tiny water droplets suspended in atmosphere near ground.', 'Reduces maritime visibility, causing lighthouses to sound foghorns.'),
    ('FOOT', 'Lower Extremity', 'Terminal part of the leg supporting body weight and facilitating walking.', 'Contains 26 bones and dozens of joints providing shock absorption.'),
    ('FOREST', 'Woodland Biome', 'Dense growth of trees and underbrush covering a large tract of land.', 'The Amazon rainforest produces massive rainfall and oxygen cycles.'),
    ('FOSSIL', 'Ancient Trace', 'Preserved remains or traces of ancient organisms petrified in rock strata.', 'Reveals prehistoric evolutionary histories and extinct ancient lineages.'),
    ('FRANC', 'Swiss Currency', 'Official currency and legal tender of Switzerland and Liechtenstein.', 'Widely regarded as a global safe-haven currency issued by the Swiss National Bank.'),
    ('FRESCO', 'Plaster Mural', 'Mural painting technique executed rapidly upon freshly laid lime plaster.', 'Michelangelo painted the Sistine Chapel ceiling using fresco pigments.'),
    ('FRICTION', 'Resistive Force', 'Force resisting the relative motion of solid surfaces, fluid layers, and material elements.', 'Converts kinetic mechanical energy into thermal waste heat when surfaces rub together.'),
    ('FUJI', 'Sacred Volcano', 'Symmetrical snow-capped active stratovolcano and highest peak in Japan.', "Sacred Shinto pilgrimage site immortalized in Hokusai's woodblock print art."),
    ('GABORONE', 'Botswana Capital', 'Capital and largest city of Botswana situated near the South African border.', "Serves as the administrative center for one of the world's leading diamond nations."),
    ('GALAXY', 'Cosmic Island', 'System of billions of stars, gas, and dark matter bound by gravity.', 'Our Solar System resides inside the barred spiral Milky Way galaxy.'),
    ('GALILEO', 'Father of Modern Science', 'Italian astronomer who pioneered telescopic observation, discovering four moons of Jupiter.', 'Championed Copernican heliocentrism, earning house arrest by the Roman Inquisition in 1633.'),
    ('GANDHI', 'Father of India', 'Indian lawyer and anti-colonial nationalist who employed nonviolent resistance for freedom.', 'Led the Salt March in 1930; inspired civil rights and freedom movements across the globe.'),
    ('GANGES', 'Sacred River', 'Trans-boundary river sacred to millions of Hindus flowing across northern India to Bengal.', 'Personified as the goddess Ganga; millions bathe in its waters at Varanasi and Haridwar.'),
    ('GENE', 'Heredity Unit', 'Basic physical unit of heredity composed of sequential DNA instructions.', 'Encodes instructions for building specific biological proteins.'),
    ('GENETICS', 'Heredity Science', 'Biological study of genes, genetic variation, and heredity in living organisms.', 'Pioneered in 1866 by Austrian monk Gregor Mendel crossbreeding garden pea plants.'),
    ('GENOME', 'Complete DNA Code', 'The complete set of genes or genetic material present in an organism.', 'The Human Genome Project mapped over three billion base pairs of DNA.'),
    ('GEORGETOWN', 'Guyanese Capital', 'Coastal port capital of Guyana known for grand wooden British colonial architecture.', "Home to the soaring wooden St. George's Cathedral and the Caribbean Community (CARICOM)."),
    ('GEYSER', 'Thermal Spout', 'Hot spring that periodically boils and erupts a tall jet of water.', 'Old Faithful in Yellowstone National Park erupts on predictable clocks.'),
    ('GIBRALTAR', 'Pillar of Hercules', 'Prominent monolithic limestone promontory on the southwestern tip of Europe.', 'Guards the narrow maritime strait linking the Atlantic Ocean to the Mediterranean Sea.'),
    ('GILGAMESH', 'Oldest Known Epic', 'Ancient Mesopotamian epic poem regarded as the earliest surviving great work of literature.', 'Follows King Gilgamesh of Uruk and wild man Enkidu in search of the secret of eternal life.'),
    ('GLACIER', 'Moving Ice River', 'Massive, persistent body of dense ice that moves slowly under its own immense weight.', 'Carves characteristic U-shaped valleys, moraines, and fjords across mountain ranges.'),
    ('GLADIATOR', 'Armed Roman Combatant', 'Armed combatant who entertained audiences in the Roman Republic and Roman Empire in violent confrontations.', 'Trained in gladiatorial schools (ludi) to fight fellow gladiators, wild beasts, and criminals.'),
    ('GOBI', 'Cold Asian Desert', 'Vast cold desert and semidesert region spanning northern China and Mongolia.', 'Site of the first discovered fossilized dinosaur eggs in the 1920s by scientists.'),
    ('GOD', 'Deity Entity', 'Superhuman being worshiped as having power over nature and humanity.', 'Revered across polytheistic and monotheistic world traditions.'),
    ('GOLD', 'Precious Metal', 'Precious yellow metallic element with atomic number 79.', 'Has symbolized wealth, purity, and beauty across cultures for millennia.'),
    ('GRAVITATION', 'Universal Attraction', 'Fundamental physical interaction by which all masses in the universe attract.', 'Sir Isaac Newton formulated the law of universal gravitation in 1687.'),
    ('GREENLAND', 'Largest Island', "The world's largest island, located between the Arctic and Atlantic Oceans, an autonomous Danish territory.", 'Covered by a massive continental ice sheet that is second in size only to Antarctica.'),
    ('GRIFFIN', 'Legendary Beast', 'Mythical creature with the head, wings, and forelegs of an eagle and the body of a lion.', 'Regarded as the king of all beasts and birds; guarded gold treasures and sacred portals.'),
    ('GUITAR', 'Plucked Stringed Instrument', 'Fretted stringed instrument typically having six strings, played by strumming or plucking.', 'Features acoustic hollow-body models and solid-body electric guitars amplified through speakers.'),
    ('GULF', 'Large Sea Inlet', 'Deep, expansive ocean inlet partially enclosed by land, larger than a bay.', 'The Gulf of Mexico is surrounded by North America and Cuba.'),
    ('GUTENBERG', 'Printing Pioneer', 'German inventor who introduced movable mechanical type printing to Europe around 1440.', 'His printed Gutenberg Bibles sparked the European Renaissance and the Protestant Reformation.'),
    ('HADES', 'Lord of the Underworld', 'Ancient Greek god of the dead and king of the underworld, brother of Zeus and Poseidon.', 'Guarded the realm of deceased souls with his three-headed watchdog Cerberus.'),
    ('HAGIASOPHIA', 'Byzantine Masterpiece', 'Historic religious monument in Istanbul, Turkey, famous for its massive soaring central dome.', 'Built in 537 AD as the patriarchal cathedral of Constantinople under Emperor Justinian I.'),
    ('HALLOWEEN', 'All Hallows Eve', 'Celebration observed on October 31 dedicated to remembering the dead and spirits.', "Celebrated with costume parties, trick-or-treating, carving pumpkin jack-o'-lanterns, and bonfires."),
    ('HAMLET', 'Tragedy of Denmark', "Shakespearean tragedy dramatizing Prince Hamlet's revenge against his uncle Claudius.", "Features famous soliloquies including 'To be, or not to be' and the gravedigger scene."),
    ('HANOI', 'Vietnamese Capital', 'Charming capital of Vietnam renowned for centuries-old architecture and lakes.', 'Features the bustling Old Quarter, Hoan Kiem Lake, and French colonial avenues.'),
    ('HARARE', 'Zimbabwean Capital', 'Sunny capital city of Zimbabwe famous for wide avenues lined with flowering jacarandas.', 'Home to the National Gallery of Zimbabwe and balancing rock geological formations.'),
    ('HARP', 'Plucked Strings', 'String instrument with vertical strings plucked with fingers in concertos.', 'The national emblem of Ireland, associated with angelic melodies.'),
    ('HAVANA', 'Cuban Capital', 'Historic Caribbean capital of Cuba famous for Spanish colonial plazas and vintage cars.', 'Features the 16th-century Castillo de la Real Fuerza and vibrant Malecón sea drive.'),
    ('HEAD', 'Cranial Portion', 'Upper anatomical division of body housing brain, eyes, and sensory organs.', 'Enclosed and shielded by the hard bony protective skull cranium.'),
    ('HEART', 'Muscular Pump', 'Muscular organ pumping oxygenated blood throughout the circulatory system.', 'Beats roughly 100,000 times each day to sustain human life.'),
    ('HELIUM', 'Inert Noble Gas', 'Light, non-reactive noble gas that is the second most abundant in cosmos.', 'Used to fill buoyant blimps and balloons; cools MRI magnets near zero.'),
    ('HELSINKI', 'Nordic Capital', 'Seaside capital of Finland celebrated for modern Nordic design and sea forts.', 'Home to the neoclassical Helsinki Cathedral and the sea fortress of Suomenlinna.'),
    ('HEMISPHERE', 'Half of the Globe', "Half of the Earth's terrestrial sphere, divided by the equator or prime meridian.", 'The Northern and Southern Hemispheres experience reversed opposing seasons.'),
    ('HERCULES', 'Mythic Strongman', 'Divine hero in Greek and Roman mythology renowned for superhuman strength and adventures.', 'Son of Zeus who successfully completed the legendary Twelve Labors, slaying the Nemean Lion.'),
    ('HERMES', 'Messenger God', 'Herald and messenger of the Greek gods, protector of travelers, merchants, and thieves.', 'Depicted wearing winged sandals (talaria) and carrying the serpent-entwined caduceus wand.'),
    ('HERO', 'Noble Champion', 'Person admired for extraordinary courage, achievements, and nobility.', 'Mythological figures who triumph over trials for the greater good.'),
    ('HIEROGLYPH', 'Ancient Egyptian Script', 'Character used in a system of pictorial writing, especially in ancient Egyptian monumental inscriptions.', 'Consisted of phonetic glyphs and logograms deciphered in 1822 using the Rosetta Stone.'),
    ('HIEROGLYPHS', 'Sacred Picture Script', 'Writing system using pictorial characters used in ancient Pharaonic Egypt.', 'Deciphered by Jean-François Champollion in 1822 using the Rosetta Stone.'),
    ('HILL', 'Natural Elevation', 'Naturally elevated area of land, smaller and less steep than a mountain.', 'Rolling green hills dot countrysides across Ireland and Tuscany.'),
    ('HOMER', 'Epic Greek Poet', 'Legendary author of the Iliad and the Odyssey, the two foundational epic poems of ancient Greece.', 'Immortalized the Trojan War, the wrath of Achilles, and the wanderings of King Odysseus.'),
    ('HURRICANE', 'Tropical Cyclone', 'Rapidly rotating storm system with a low-pressure center, strong winds, and heavy spiral rainbands.', 'Categorized on the Saffir-Simpson wind scale from Category 1 up to Category 5.'),
    ('HYDRA', 'Multi-Headed Water Serpent', 'Serpentine water monster in Greek and Roman mythology with multiple heads that regenerated when cut.', 'Slain by Hercules as his second labor, using burning torches to cauterize neck stumps.'),
    ('ICE', 'Frozen Water', 'Solid crystalline state of water formed when temperature drops below 0°C.', 'Floats on water because its crystalline lattice is less dense than liquid.'),
    ('ICEBERG', 'Floating Freshwater', 'Colossal chunk of freshwater ice that has calved from a glacier and floats in open sea.', "Roughly ninety percent of an iceberg's total volume remains submerged beneath the water."),
    ('ICELAND', 'Land of Fire and Ice', 'Nordic island country in the North Atlantic defined by its dramatic volcanic and glacial landscape.', 'Features active geysers, hot geothermal springs, lava fields, and massive glaciers.'),
    ('IGUAZU', 'Thunder Cataracts', 'Stunning chain of 275 waterfalls along the border of Argentina and Brazil.', "Features the semi-circular Devil's Throat cataract where thundering water plumes mist high."),
    ('ILIAD', 'Trojan War Epic', 'Ancient Greek epic poem by Homer set during the final weeks of the Trojan War siege.', 'Chronicles the quarrel between King Agamemnon and the invincible warrior hero Achilles.'),
    ('INDEPENDENCE', 'Self-Governance', 'Condition of a nation establishing self-governance and freedom from colonial rule.', 'Celebrated with national independence holidays, parades, and fireworks.'),
    ('INDUSTRIAL', 'Manufacturing Transformation', 'Relating to the transformative historical revolution that replaced manual work with machine factories.', 'Began in 18th-century Britain with steam engines, mechanized cotton mills, and iron smelting.'),
    ('INERTIA', 'Resistance to Change', 'Property of matter by which it continues in its existing state of rest or uniform motion.', "Newton's First Law of Motion states objects maintain velocity unless acted on by force."),
    ('INFERNO', 'Nine Circles of Hell', "First part of Italian writer Dante Alighieri's 14th-century epic poem Divine Comedy.", 'Follows Dante guided by the Roman poet Virgil through the nine circles of Hell.'),
    ('INK', 'Writing Fluid', 'Colored fluid or paste containing pigments used for writing and printing.', 'Ancient Egyptians and Chinese developed ink using soot and binders.'),
    ('INSCRIPTION', 'Carved Words', 'Words, names, or decrees inscribed into monument stone, metal plates, or tablets.', 'Provides durable historical records surviving thousands of years of weather.'),
    ('IRON', 'Base Metal', 'Strong metallic element that revolutionized ancient toolmaking and steel.', 'The Iron Age brought mass manufacturing of plows, tools, and armor.'),
    ('ISLAND', 'Surrounded Land', 'Tract of land completely surrounded by water, smaller than a continent.', 'Greenland is the largest non-continental island on planet Earth.'),
    ('ISLE', 'Small Island', 'Island, especially one of small size, surrounded by open waters.', 'Scenic rocky isles dot the coastlines of Scotland and Greece.'),
    ('ISOTOPE', 'Nuclear Variant', 'Variants of a particular chemical element which differ in neutron number within nuclei.', 'Carbon-14 is an unstable radioactive isotope used in archaeological radiocarbon dating.'),
    ('ISTHMUS', 'Narrow Land Bridge', 'Narrow strip of land connecting two larger land masses, with water on both sides.', 'The Isthmus of Panama connects North and South America, pierced by the Panama Canal.'),
    ('JAKARTA', 'Indonesian Capital', 'Massive capital of Indonesia situated on the northwest coast of the island of Java.', 'Historic melting pot of Malay, Javanese, Arab, Chinese, and European cultures.'),
    ('JERUSALEM', 'Holy City', 'Historic city sacred to three Abrahamic faiths: Judaism, Christianity, and Islam.', 'Encloses the Western Wall, Church of the Holy Sepulchre, and the Dome of the Rock.'),
    ('JUNGLE', 'Tropical Tangle', 'Dense, tangled tropical rainforest with thick vegetation at ground level.', 'Home to monkeys, jaguars, vibrant parrots, and towering emergent trees.'),
    ('JUPITER', 'Giant Gas Planet', 'The largest planet in our Solar System, with mass more than twice all other planets combined.', 'Famous for its swirling Great Red Spot storm and dozens of moons including Europa.'),
    ('JURISDICTION', 'Legal Authority', 'The official power and territorial boundary to make legal decisions and judgments.', 'Defines the geographical and subject matter limits of courts and police authority.'),
    ('KALAHARI', 'Southern Desert', 'Large semi-arid sandy savannah basin covering parts of Botswana and Namibia.', 'Home to the San Bushmen people, meerkats, and desert-adapted wildlife.'),
    ('KAMPALA', 'Ugandan Capital', 'Hilly capital city of Uganda situated near the shores of vast Lake Victoria.', 'Built across historic rolling hills; home to the UNESCO-listed Kasubi Tombs.'),
    ('KIGALI', 'Rwandan Capital', 'Clean, hilly capital city of Rwanda known as the Singapore of Africa.', 'Renowned for modern convention centers, tech innovation, and civic cleanliness.'),
    ('KILIMANJARO', 'African Roof Peak', 'Dormant volcanic mountain in Tanzania, the highest peak in Africa at 19,341 feet.', 'Features three volcanic cones: Kibo, Mawenzi, and Shira, crowned by alpine glaciers.'),
    ('KING', 'Male Sovereign', 'Male monarch ruling over a kingdom, usually inheriting royal lineage.', 'Governs state affairs from a throne, wearing a royal crown.'),
    ('KINGSTON', 'Jamaican Capital', 'Cultural and commercial capital of Jamaica situated beneath the Blue Mountains.', 'The global birthplace of reggae music, ska, and dub; home to the Bob Marley Museum.'),
    ('KNIGHT', 'Medieval Armored Warrior', 'Person granted an honorary title of knighthood by a monarch for military service, clad in armor.', 'Followed the chivalric code of honor and fought with sword, lance, and shield on horseback.'),
    ('KRAKATOA', 'Explosive Caldera', 'Indonesian volcanic island famous for a catastrophic explosion in 1883.', 'The 1883 eruption produced the loudest sound recorded in human history, heard 3,000 miles away.'),
    ('KREMLIN', 'Russian Citadel', 'Fortified historic complex at the heart of Moscow overlooking the Moskva River and Red Square.', 'Serves as the official residence of the President of Russia and houses ancient cathedrals.'),
    ('KRONA', 'Swedish Currency', 'Official currency of Sweden since the monetary union of 1873.', 'Represented by the code SEK; subdivided historically into 100 öre.'),
    ('KRONE', 'Scandinavian Currency', 'Official currency name of both Norway and Denmark.', 'Derived from the Scandinavian word for crown; backed by respective central banks.'),
    ('LAGOON', 'Shallow Saltwater', 'Shallow body of water separated from a larger sea by barrier islands or coral reefs.', 'Features tranquil, calm turquoise waters sheltered from rough open ocean swells.'),
    ('LAGOS', 'Commercial Megacity', 'The most populous metropolitan city in Nigeria and major financial hub of Africa.', 'Renowned for Nollywood cinema industries, bustling markets, and tech start-ups.'),
    ('LAKE', 'Inland Water', 'Large body of freshwater or saltwater completely surrounded by land.', 'Lake Baikal in Siberia is the deepest freshwater lake on planet Earth.'),
    ('LAPAZ', 'Andean Seat', 'The highest administrative capital in the world, sitting at 11,975 feet in Bolivia.', 'Connected by an innovative network of aerial cable car transit lines called Mi Teleférico.'),
    ('LAVA', 'Molten Rock', 'Hot molten or semi-fluid rock erupted from a volcano or fissure.', 'Cools into dark igneous basalt rock upon contact with air or sea.'),
    ('LAW', 'Legal Order', 'System of enforceable rules established by a governing authority.', 'Codified in historic tablets like the ancient Code of Hammurabi.'),
    ('LEAD', 'Heavy Element', 'Heavy, malleable, soft bluish-grey metal with atomic number 82.', 'Historically used in Roman plumbing; absorbs ionizing radiation.'),
    ('LEGION', 'Roman Brigade', 'Major unit of the ancient Roman army consisting of thousands of infantry.', 'Roman legionaries conquered the Mediterranean using discipline and shields.'),
    ('LEONARDO', 'Renaissance Genius', 'Italian Renaissance polymath celebrated for painting the Mona Lisa and visionary inventions.', 'Designed conceptual flying machines, armored tanks, and dissected human cadavers for anatomy.'),
    ('LIMA', 'Gastronomic Capital', 'Pacific coastal capital of Peru celebrated as the culinary capital of South America.', 'Home to pre-Incan adobe pyramids, Spanish colonial cathedrals, and fresh ceviche.'),
    ('LINCOLN', 'The Great Emancipator', 'Sixteenth President of the United States who preserved the Union through the American Civil War.', 'Issued the historic Emancipation Proclamation in 1863 and delivered the Gettysburg Address.'),
    ('LIRA', 'Turkish Currency', 'Official currency of Turkey and Northern Cyprus, issued by the Central Bank of Turkey.', 'Subdivided into 100 kuruş; symbolized by the stylized currency sign ₺.'),
    ('LISBON', 'City of Seven Hills', 'Coastal capital of Portugal famous for sun-drenched hills and historic trams.', 'Features the 16th-century Belém Tower and Jerónimos Monastery on Tagus River.'),
    ('LOKI', 'Norse Trickster God', 'Trickster god in Norse mythology known for shapeshifting and cunning mischief.', 'Father of the Fenrir wolf, Midgard serpent Jormungandr, and the eight-legged steed Sleipnir.'),
    ('LONDON', 'Historic Capital', 'Capital of the United Kingdom situated along the River Thames.', 'Features Big Ben, the Tower of London, Buckingham Palace, and Westminster Abbey.'),
    ('LORD', 'Noble Title', 'Title given to a peer of the realm, nobleman, or feudal landowner.', 'Historically sat in the British parliamentary House of Lords.'),
    ('LOUVRE', 'Grand Art Museum', "The world's most-visited art museum, housed in a historic royal palace in Paris.", "Displays Leonardo da Vinci's Mona Lisa, Venus de Milo, and Winged Victory of Samothrace."),
    ('LUNG', 'Breathing Organ', 'Pair of respiratory organs in chest that exchange oxygen with blood.', 'Contains millions of microscopic alveoli sacs for gas exchange.'),
    ('LUTE', 'Fretted Strings', 'Plucked string instrument with a pear-shaped back popular in Renaissance.', 'Central instrument for domestic music-making across Europe for centuries.'),
    ('MACBETH', 'Scottish Play of Ambition', 'Shakespearean tragedy recounting the bloody rise and fall of the ambitious Scottish general Macbeth.', 'Prophesied by three witches and spurred by Lady Macbeth; features the haunting dagger vision.'),
    ('MACHUPICCHU', 'Lost Inca City', '15th-century Inca citadel situated on an Andean mountain ridge in Peru above Urubamba.', 'Built with polished dry-stone walls fit so tightly that a knife blade cannot fit between.'),
    ('MADAGASCAR', 'Biodiverse Island', 'Large island country situated off the southeastern coast of Africa in the Indian Ocean.', 'Famous for unique endemic wildlife, including dozens of lemur species and baobab trees.'),
    ('MADRID', 'Spanish Capital', 'Central capital of Spain renowned for royal palaces and classical art museums.', 'Home to the Prado Museum, expansive Retiro Park, and the grand Plaza Mayor.'),
    ('MAGELLAN', 'Circumnavigator', 'Portuguese explorer whose Spanish expedition achieved the first recorded global circumnavigation.', "Discovered the Strait of Magellan at South America's tip; expedition led home by Juan Elcano."),
    ('MAGNET', 'Field Source', 'Material or object that produces an invisible magnetic field attracting iron.', 'Possesses North and South poles; opposite magnetic poles attract.'),
    ('MAGNETISM', 'Magnetic Force', 'Class of physical phenomena that are mediated by magnetic fields produced by currents.', 'Opposite magnetic poles attract each other, while like magnetic poles repel each other.'),
    ('MANAGUA', 'Nicaraguan Capital', 'Lakeside capital of Nicaragua situated on the southern shores of Lake Xolotlán.', 'Surrounded by volcanic crater lagoons and rich revolutionary political history.'),
    ('MANDELA', 'Anti-Apartheid Leader', "South African anti-apartheid revolutionary and statesman who became country's first black president.", 'Spent 27 years imprisoned on Robben Island before leading reconciliation and winning Nobel Peace Prize.'),
    ('MANGROVE', 'Tidal Wetland Forest', 'Salt-tolerant coastal forest tree adapted to growing in brackish intertidal swamp water.', 'Stilt prop roots trap sediments, buffering coastlines against catastrophic hurricanes.'),
    ('MANILA', 'Pearl of the Orient', 'Bayside capital of the Philippines known for Spanish colonial architecture in Intramuros.', 'Features historic Fort Santiago, San Agustin Church, and colorful passenger jeepneys.'),
    ('MAP', 'Cartography', 'Visual diagram or representation of an area of land or sea showing features.', 'Uses coordinates, compass roses, and scales to guide navigation.'),
    ('MAPUTO', 'Mozambican Capital', 'Port capital of Mozambique situated on the calm waters of Maputo Bay.', 'Renowned for wide avenues lined with acacia trees, Mediterranean architecture, and seafood.'),
    ('MARS', 'The Red Planet', 'Fourth planet from the Sun known as the Red Planet due to oxidized iron dust on surface.', 'Home to Olympus Mons, the largest volcano in the Solar System, and frozen polar ice caps.'),
    ('MATTERHORN', 'Pyramid Mountain', 'Iconic pyramid-shaped peak straddling the border between Switzerland and Italy.', 'Its four steep faces correspond to the four cardinal directions; famous alpine icon.'),
    ('MEDITERRANEAN', 'Inland Sea Basin', 'Vast sea basin connecting Europe, Africa, and Asia through the Strait of Gibraltar.', 'Cradle of maritime civilizations that pioneered philosophy, maritime trade, and wine.'),
    ('MEKONG', 'Southeast Asian River', 'Trans-boundary river flowing through China, Myanmar, Laos, Thailand, Cambodia, and Vietnam.', "Supports one of the world's most productive inland freshwater fisheries and rice deltas."),
    ('MERCURY', 'Innermost Planet', 'The smallest planet in the Solar System and closest to the Sun.', 'Has virtually no atmosphere; surface temperatures swing from 800°F by day to -290°F at night.'),
    ('MERMAID', 'Aquatic Mythic Maiden', 'Mythical aquatic creature with the head and upper body of a woman and the tail of a fish.', 'Appears across worldwide folklore, singing bewitching songs to sailors from ocean rocks.'),
    ('METEOR', 'Shooting Star', 'Streak of glowing light produced when space debris burns in atmosphere.', 'Annual meteor showers like the Perseids illuminate summer night skies.'),
    ('METEOROLOGY', 'Weather Science', 'Branch of science concerned with the processes and phenomena of the atmosphere.', 'Uses Doppler radar, satellite imaging, and supercomputers to forecast weather.'),
    ('METROPOLIS', 'Major Urban Hub', 'Vast, populous, and bustling capital city or central economic urban hub.', 'Global metropolises like Tokyo, London, and New York drive international commerce.'),
    ('MEXICO', 'Historic Megacity', 'Sprawling historic capital of Mexico built atop the ancient Aztec capital of Tenochtitlan.', 'Home to the massive Zócalo plaza, the Metropolitan Cathedral, and Chapultepec Park.'),
    ('MICHELANGELO', 'Master Sculptor', 'Italian sculptor, painter, and architect of the High Renaissance who painted the Sistine Chapel.', "Sculpted the marble masterpieces of David and the Pietà; designed St. Peter's Basilica dome."),
    ('MILKYWAY', 'Home Galaxy', 'Barred spiral galaxy containing our Solar System and hundreds of billions of stars.', 'Appears across dark night skies as a hazy luminous band of glowing starlight.'),
    ('MINOTAUR', 'Labyrinth Monster', 'Mythical monster with the head of a bull and body of a man trapped in the Cretan labyrinth.', "King Minos kept him inside Daedalus's maze until slain by the Athenian prince Theseus."),
    ('MISSISSIPPI', 'Great American River', 'Chief river of the second-largest drainage system on the North American continent.', 'Flows 2,340 miles southward from Lake Itasca in Minnesota to the Gulf of Mexico.'),
    ('MIST', 'Fine Water Cloud', 'Phenomenon of small water droplets suspended in air, lighter than fog.', 'Drapes morning mountain valleys and surrounds thundering waterfalls.'),
    ('MITOCHONDRIA', 'Cellular Generator', 'Membrane-bound cellular organelles generating chemical adenosine triphosphate.', 'Known as the powerhouse of the cell, carrying its own circular DNA genome.'),
    ('MOJAVE', 'Joshua Tree Desert', 'Arid desert region in the southwestern US characterized by iconic Joshua trees.', 'Contains Death Valley, the lowest, driest, and hottest location in North America.'),
    ('MOMENTUM', 'Mass in Motion', 'The quantity of motion of a moving body, measured as a product of its mass and velocity.', 'A fundamental conserved quantity in physics that cannot be created or destroyed.'),
    ('MONSOON', 'Seasonal Wind Shift', 'Seasonal reversing wind pattern accompanied by corresponding changes in precipitation.', 'Brings essential annual rainy seasons to the Indian subcontinent and Southeast Asia.'),
    ('MONTBLANC', 'Highest Alps Peak', 'The highest mountain in the Alps and Western Europe, rising 15,777 feet.', 'Snow-capped massif straddling France and Italy, popular for alpine mountaineering.'),
    ('MONTEVIDEO', 'Uruguayan Capital', 'Coastal capital of Uruguay known for seaside promenades and colonial plazas.', 'Features the 13-mile Rambla coastal walk along the Atlantic and rich soccer history.'),
    ('MOON', 'Natural Satellite', 'The natural celestial body orbiting Earth, driving ocean tides.', 'Its gravitational pull causes daily ocean high and low tides.'),
    ('MOSAIC', 'Tiled Artwork', 'Art picture produced by arranging small colored pieces of stone or glass.', 'Ancient Roman villas featured intricate decorative mosaic tile floors.'),
    ('MOSCOW', 'Russian Capital', 'Historic capital of Russia situated on the Moskva River in Eastern Europe.', "Famous for the fortified Kremlin complex, Red Square, and Saint Basil's Cathedral."),
    ('MOZART', 'Musical Prodigy', 'Prolific and influential Austrian classical composer who began composing at five years old.', 'Composed over 600 masterworks including The Magic Flute, Don Giovanni, and his Requiem.'),
    ('MUD', 'Wet Earth', 'Soft, sticky matter resulting from the mixing of earth and water.', 'Ancient civilizations molded sun-dried mud bricks to build homes.'),
    ('MUSEUM', 'Cultural Vault', 'Institution storing and exhibiting objects of historical and artistic value.', 'The Louvre in Paris displays the Mona Lisa and classical antiquities.'),
    ('MYTH', 'Ancient Lore', 'Traditional sacred story concerning gods, supernatural heroes, and origins.', 'Explains natural phenomena, cosmic creation, and societal customs.'),
    ('NAIROBI', 'Kenyan Capital', "Dynamic capital of Kenya known as the 'Green City in the Sun'.", 'Features Nairobi National Park where wild lions roam before city skyscrapers.'),
    ('NAPOLEON', 'French Emperor', 'French military commander and emperor who conquered much of continental Europe in 1800s.', 'Established the Napoleonic Code legal system before final military defeat at the Battle of Waterloo.'),
    ('NASSAU', 'Bahamian Capital', 'Vibrant island capital of the Bahamas situated on New Providence Island.', 'Famous for historic pink colonial parliament buildings and crystal-clear turquoise waters.'),
    ('NEBULA', 'Star Nursery', 'Interstellar cloud of gas and dust where new baby stars are born.', 'The Orion Nebula is a vibrant star-forming region visible to naked eyes.'),
    ('NEPTUNE', 'Windswept Ice Giant', 'The outermost planet in the Solar System, known for intense supersonic winds.', 'Features deep azure blue color, a dynamic Great Dark Spot storm, and geyser moon Triton.'),
    ('NEWDELHI', 'Indian Capital', 'Federal capital city of India renowned for grand Mughal and colonial monuments.', "Home to the Red Fort, India Gate war memorial, Humayun's Tomb, and Lotus Temple."),
    ('NEWTON', 'Classical Physicist', 'English mathematician and physicist who formulated the laws of motion and universal gravity.', 'Invented calculus and the reflecting telescope; authored the landmark Principia Mathematica.'),
    ('NIAGARA', 'Mighty Cataracts', 'Group of three massive waterfalls straddling the international border of the US and Canada.', 'Composed of Horseshoe Falls, American Falls, and Bridal Veil Falls, powering huge turbines.'),
    ('NILE', 'Historic African River', 'Famous north-flowing river in northeastern Africa traditionally considered the longest.', 'Its annual summer floodwaters deposited nutrient-rich silt that sustained ancient Egyptian civilization.'),
    ('NOSE', 'Olfactory Sense', 'Facial organ housing nasal cavities for breathing and smelling.', 'Detects thousands of distinct airborne chemical odor molecules.'),
    ('NOTE', 'Musical Tone', 'Symbol representing a specific musical pitch and duration on a staff.', 'Forms the building blocks of musical chords, scales, and melodies.'),
    ('NOVEL', 'Prose Fiction Book', 'Fictitious prose narrative of substantial length and complexity depicting human experience.', 'Examples include Don Quixote, Pride and Prejudice, War and Peace, and Moby-Dick.'),
    ('NUCLEI', 'Atomic Centers', 'Plural of nucleus; the dense central cores of atoms holding nucleons.', 'Contain positively charged protons and electrically neutral neutrons.'),
    ('NUCLEUS', 'Atomic Core', 'The dense, positively charged central core of an atom containing protons and neutrons.', 'Discovered by Ernest Rutherford in 1911 through the gold foil alpha-particle experiment.'),
    ('OAK', 'Hardwood Tree', 'Stately deciduous tree species famous for durable timber and acorns.', 'Historically utilized in ship construction and wine aging barrels.'),
    ('OASIS', 'Desert Spring', 'Isolated fertile area in a desert providing fresh water that sustains vegetation.', 'Fed by subterranean natural aquifers, allowing date palms and nomadic caravans to rest.'),
    ('OCEANOGRAPHY', 'Marine Science', 'The exploration and scientific study of physical, chemical, and biological ocean phenomena.', 'Maps abyssal ocean trenches, global oceanic currents, and hydrothermal vent ecology.'),
    ('OCEANS', 'Global Seas', 'Vast bodies of salt water that cover seventy percent of the globe.', 'Encompasses the Pacific, Atlantic, Indian, Southern, and Arctic oceans.'),
    ('ODIN', 'The Allfather', 'Widely revered god in Germanic mythology and king of the Norse gods in Asgard.', "Sacrificed one eye at Mimir's well for universal wisdom; accompanied by ravens Huginn and Muninn."),
    ('ODYSSEY', 'Epic Voyage', 'Ancient Greek epic poem attributed to Homer chronicling the ten-year journey home of Odysseus.', 'Features encounters with the Cyclops Polyphemus, Circe the sorceress, and the Sirens.'),
    ('OKTOBERFEST', 'Bavarian Folk Festival', "World's largest folk festival held annually in Munich, Bavaria, celebrating German culture.", 'Features massive beer tents, traditional brass music, lederhosen, dirndls, and pretzels.'),
    ('OPERA', 'Theatrical Music Drama', 'Theatrical art form in which dramatic singers and musicians perform a dramatic work.', 'Blends acting, scenery, costumes, and orchestral music; famous in Italian and German traditions.'),
    ('OPTICS', 'Light Physics', 'Branch of physics studying the behavior, properties, and lenses of light.', 'Underpins telescopes, microscopes, fiber-optic cables, and cameras.'),
    ('ORGANISM', 'Living Entity', 'Individual animal, plant, bacterium, or single-celled life form capable of response.', 'Undergoes biological metabolism, maintains internal homeostasis, and reproduces.'),
    ('ORION', 'The Hunter', "Prominent winter constellation recognizable by the three bright stars of Orion's Belt.", 'Contains the red supergiant star Betelgeuse and the brilliant blue supergiant Rigel.'),
    ('OSIRIS', 'Egyptian Lord of Dead', 'Ancient Egyptian god of the afterlife, death, resurrection, and vegetative fertility.', 'Depicted as a green-skinned pharaoh wrapped in mummy linens holding the crook and flail.'),
    ('OSLO', 'Norwegian Capital', 'Coastal capital of Norway surrounded by dense pine forests and scenic fjords.', 'Home to the Nobel Peace Center, Vigeland Sculpture Park, and Viking Ship Museum.'),
    ('OTTAWA', 'Canadian Capital', 'Bilingual capital city of Canada situated along the Ottawa River in Ontario.', "Home to Parliament Hill's Gothic towers and the UNESCO-listed Rideau Canal."),
    ('OXYGEN', 'Breath of Life', 'Chemical element with atomic number 8 essential for aerobic respiration.', "Makes up roughly 21% of Earth's atmosphere and 89% of water by mass."),
    ('PACIFIC', 'Deepest Ocean', "The largest and deepest of Earth's oceanic divisions, covering over 63 million square miles.", 'Contains the Mariana Trench and the geologically active volcano Ring of Fire.'),
    ('PAGE', 'Paper Leaf', 'Single leaf of paper in a book, manuscript, or printed document.', 'Numbered sequentially to organize written knowledge.'),
    ('PALACE', 'Royal Residence', 'Grand official residence of a sovereign monarch, ruler, or dignitary.', 'The Palace of Versailles in France features opulent halls and gardens.'),
    ('PALEONTOLOGY', 'Fossil Excavation', 'Scientific study of prehistoric life through the examination of fossils.', 'Reconstructs the anatomy, diet, and behavior of ancient extinct dinosaurs.'),
    ('PANAMA', 'Canal Capital', 'Modern skyscraper capital of Panama situated at the Pacific entrance of the Panama Canal.', 'Blends gleaming high-rise bank towers with the colonial cobbled streets of Casco Viejo.'),
    ('PAPYRUS', 'Ancient Writing Material', 'Material prepared in ancient Egypt from the pithy stem of a water plant, used for writing documents.', 'Strips were layered perpendicularly, pressed, and dried to form flexible scroll sheets.'),
    ('PARAMARIBO', 'Surinamese Capital', 'Historic wooden capital city of Suriname situated along the Suriname River.', 'Its historic inner city features a unique fusion of Dutch architecture and indigenous timber.'),
    ('PARCHMENT', 'Animal Skin Writing Surface', 'Writing material made from specially prepared untanned skins of sheep, calves, or goats.', 'Used extensively throughout antiquity and the Middle Ages to create illuminated manuscripts.'),
    ('PARIS', 'City of Light', 'Capital of France celebrated for art, fashion, gastronomy, and the Eiffel Tower.', 'Home to the Louvre Museum, Notre-Dame Cathedral, and the Champs-Élysées avenue.'),
    ('PARLIAMENT', 'Legislative Body', 'Legislative assembly of elected representatives that debates and enacts laws.', 'The British Parliament consists of the House of Commons and House of Lords.'),
    ('PARTHENON', 'Athenian Temple', 'Former temple on the Athenian Acropolis dedicated to the Greek goddess Athena.', 'Constructed in 447 BC; celebrated for its classical Doric marble architecture.'),
    ('PAST', 'Elapsed Time', 'Events and periods of time that occurred prior to the present moment.', 'Studied through written historical accounts and archaeological finds.'),
    ('PEAK', 'Mountain Summit', 'The pointed top of a mountain, or reaching the highest athletic state.', 'Mountaineers strive to stand upon remote, snow-capped alpine peaks.'),
    ('PEGASUS', 'Winged Stallion', 'Pure white winged divine stallion in Greek mythology sired by Poseidon.', 'Bellerophon rode Pegasus to slay the fire-breathing Chimera monster in Lycia.'),
    ('PEN', 'Writing Tool', 'Handheld instrument used to apply ink to paper for writing and drawing.', 'Includes historic feather quills, fountain pens, and ballpoints.'),
    ('PENINSULA', 'Surrounded Land', 'Piece of land surrounded by water on three sides while connected to mainland.', 'Prominent examples include the Iberian Peninsula, Florida, and the Italian boot.'),
    ('PESO', 'Latin American Currency', 'Monetary unit of Mexico, Argentina, Colombia, Chile, and the Philippines.', 'Originates from the historic Spanish silver dollar piece of eight (peso de ocho).'),
    ('PETRA', 'Rose-Red City', 'Historic archaeological city in southern Jordan famous for rock-cut architecture.', 'Carved directly into red sandstone cliff faces by the Nabataean kingdom in 300 BC.'),
    ('PHARAOH', 'Ancient Egyptian Monarch', 'Title used for monarch rulers of ancient Egypt from the First Dynasty until Roman annexation.', 'Regarded as divine intermediaries between the gods and humanity; buried in grand tombs.'),
    ('PHILOSOPHER', 'Wisdom Thinker', 'Person who seeks wisdom and enlightenment through rigorous philosophical inquiry.', 'Probes questions of morality, existence, logic, consciousness, and human knowledge.'),
    ('PHILOSOPHY', 'Love of Wisdom', 'Systematic study of fundamental questions about existence, knowledge, values, and mind.', "Derived from the Greek words 'philo' (love) and 'sophia' (wisdom)."),
    ('PHOENIX', 'Immortal Firebird', 'Immortal mythical firebird that cyclically regenerates by rising anew from its own ashes.', 'Associated with the sun; lives for centuries before peacefully bursting into fragrant flames.'),
    ('PHOTON', 'Light Particle', 'Elementary particle representing a single quantum of light and radiation.', 'Travels at 186,282 miles per second in vacuum, carrying energy.'),
    ('PHOTOSYNTHESIS', 'Solar Food Synthesis', 'Process used by green plants to convert solar sunlight into chemical sugars.', 'Releases life-sustaining oxygen as a byproduct while capturing atmospheric carbon.'),
    ('PIANO', 'Acoustic Keyboard Instrument', 'Acoustic stringed keyboard instrument where felt-covered hammers strike tuned metal strings.', 'Invented in Italy by Bartolomeo Cristofori around the year 1700; features 88 keys.'),
    ('PLANET', 'Celestial Body', 'Astronomical body orbiting a star massive enough to be rounded by gravity.', 'The eight recognized planets in our Solar System orbit the Sun.'),
    ('PLANTS', 'Flora Kingdom', 'Multicellular photosynthetic organisms characterized by cell walls.', 'Produce life-sustaining oxygen and sugars while capturing sunlight.'),
    ('PLASMA', 'Fourth State', 'Ionized gas consisting of equal numbers of positive ions and electrons.', 'The most common state of ordinary matter in the universe, seen in stars.'),
    ('PLATEAU', 'Elevated Flatland', 'Vast area of elevated, relatively flat land rising sharply above surrounding areas.', "The Tibetan Plateau is known as the 'Roof of the World', averaging 14,800 feet in height."),
    ('PLATO', 'Athenian Thinker', 'Ancient Greek philosopher who founded the Academy in Athens, student of Socrates.', 'Authored the Republic exploring justice, ideal state governance, and the Allegory of the Cave.'),
    ('PLUTO', 'Dwarf Planet', 'Dwarf planet in the Kuiper belt discovered in 1930 and reclassified by IAU in 2006.', "Visited by NASA's New Horizons probe in 2015, revealing heart-shaped nitrogen glaciers."),
    ('POEM', 'Verse Literature', 'Literary work expressing feelings and ideas with rhythm, rhyme, and meter.', 'Mastered by poets like Shakespeare, Frost, and Keats.'),
    ('POSEIDON', 'God of the Sea', 'Olympian god of the sea, earthquakes, tsunamis, and horses in Greek mythology.', 'Wields a powerful three-pronged trident capable of shattering rocks and raising tidal waves.'),
    ('POUND', 'British Sterling', 'Official currency of the United Kingdom and oldest currency still in continuous active use.', 'Represented by the pound sign (£) and issued by the Bank of England.'),
    ('PRAGUE', 'City of a Hundred Spires', 'Capital of the Czech Republic renowned for bridges, castles, and Gothic towers.', 'Features the 14th-century Charles Bridge, Prague Castle, and Astronomical Clock.'),
    ('PRESSURE', 'Force per Area', 'Continuous physical force exerted on or against an object by something in contact with it.', 'Measured in pascals, bars, or pounds per square inch (PSI) across fluid systems.'),
    ('PRETORIA', 'Executive Capital', 'Administrative executive capital of South Africa known for purple jacaranda trees.', 'Home to the historic Union Buildings and the giant bronze statue of Nelson Mandela.'),
    ('PROMETHEUS', 'Titan Fire Giver', 'Titan who defied Zeus by stealing celestial fire from Mount Olympus to gift to humanity.', 'Punished by being chained to a Caucasus mountain rock where an eagle daily ate his liver.'),
    ('PROTEIN', 'Amino Acid Chain', 'Large biomolecules consisting of one or more long chains of amino acid residues.', 'Performs vital functions in bodies including structural tissue, enzyme catalysis, and immunity.'),
    ('PROTON', 'Positive Charge', 'Stable subatomic particle with positive charge in atomic nuclei.', 'The number of protons determines the atomic number of an element.'),
    ('PULSAR', 'Ticking Star', 'Rapidly rotating neutron star emitting beams of electromagnetic pulses.', 'Acts as an ultra-precise cosmic lighthouse ticking across space.'),
    ('PYRAMID', 'Ancient Monument', 'Monumental stone structure with a square base and triangular sides meeting at an apex.', 'The Great Pyramid of Giza was built as a tomb for Pharaoh Khufu over 4,500 years ago.'),
    ('PYTHAGORAS', 'Geometric Master', 'Ancient Ionian Greek philosopher and mathematician famous for his right-triangle theorem.', 'Proved that the square of the hypotenuse equals the sum of the squares of the other two sides.'),
    ('QUARKS', 'Subatomic Units', 'Elementary particles that combine to form protons and neutrons.', 'Possess fractional electric charges and exist in six exotic flavors.'),
    ('QUASAR', 'Cosmic Powerhouse', 'Extremely luminous active galactic nucleus powered by a black hole.', 'Emits brilliant radiation thousands of times brighter than ordinary galaxies.'),
    ('QUITO', 'High-Altitude Capital', 'Historic capital of Ecuador, the second-highest official capital city on Earth.', 'Its remarkably preserved Spanish colonial historic center was the first UNESCO site.'),
    ('RABAT', 'Moroccan Capital', 'Atlantic coastal capital city of Morocco famous for historic royal architecture.', 'Features the 12th-century Hassan Tower and the picturesque Kasbah of the Udayas.'),
    ('RADIATION', 'Energy Emission', 'Emission or transmission of energy in the form of waves or particles through space.', 'Encompasses harmless radio waves, visible rainbow light, and high-energy ionizing gamma rays.'),
    ('RADIUM', 'Radioactive Metal', 'Radioactive alkaline earth metal discovered by Marie and Pierre Curie.', 'Historically glowed in the dark on luminous vintage watch dials.'),
    ('RAND', 'South African Currency', 'Official legal tender currency of South Africa, Namibia, Lesotho, and Eswatini.', 'Introduced in 1961 upon the establishment of the Republic of South Africa.'),
    ('REAL', 'Brazilian Currency', 'Official currency of Brazil introduced in 1994 as part of the Plano Real stabilization.', 'Represented by R$ and subdivided into 100 centavos; features native Brazilian fauna.'),
    ('REALM', 'Kingdom Domain', 'Territory or kingdom ruled by a sovereign monarch or sovereign government.', 'Encompasses the lands, citizens, and laws of an empire.'),
    ('REEF', 'Coral Ridge', 'Ridge of jagged rock, coral, or sand at or near the surface of the sea.', 'The Great Barrier Reef in Australia is the largest living coral reef.'),
    ('RELATIVITY', 'Einstein Spacetime', 'Physical theory formulated by Albert Einstein describing gravity and spacetime.', 'Special relativity establishes that nothing can travel faster than the speed of light.'),
    ('RENAISSANCE', 'Cultural Revival', 'The fervent period of European cultural and artistic rebirth from 14th to 17th century.', 'Witnessed groundbreaking advancements in perspective painting, anatomy, and science.'),
    ('REVOLUTION', 'Sudden Upheaval', 'Fundamental, sudden change in political power or social organizational structures.', 'The French Revolution of 1789 abolished the monarchy and established human rights.'),
    ('REYKJAVIK', 'Northernmost Capital', "The world's northernmost sovereign capital, coastal capital of Iceland.", 'Powered entirely by clean geothermal energy; home to the futuristic Harpa Concert Hall.'),
    ('RHINE', 'German River', 'Major European river flowing from the Swiss Alps through Germany to the North Sea.', 'Lined with medieval hilltop castles and terraced vineyards in the Rhine Gorge.'),
    ('RIVERS', 'Flowing Streams', 'Natural flowing watercourses heading toward an ocean, sea, or lake.', 'Historic rivers like the Nile and Tigris nurtured human civilization.'),
    ('RIYADH', 'Desert Capital', 'Booming desert capital of Saudi Arabia and financial powerhouse of the peninsula.', 'Features modern skyscrapers like Kingdom Centre rising above historic mud-brick forts.'),
    ('ROAD', 'Paved Route', 'Wide paved way leading between places for vehicular and foot transit.', 'Roman military roads connected distant provinces across Europe.'),
    ('ROCK', 'Solid Mineral', 'Naturally occurring solid aggregate of one or more minerals.', 'Classified into igneous, sedimentary, and metamorphic rock types.'),
    ('ROME', 'The Eternal City', 'Capital of Italy and historic center of the ancient Roman Empire.', 'Encloses the Colosseum, Roman Forum, Trevi Fountain, and the independent Vatican City.'),
    ('ROSETTA', 'Ancient Deciphering Stone', 'Granodiorite stele inscribed with three versions of a decree issued in Memphis, Egypt in 196 BC.', 'Inscribed in Ancient Egyptian hieroglyphic, Demotic script, and Ancient Greek, unlocking ancient texts.'),
    ('RUBLE', 'Russian Currency', 'Official currency of the Russian Federation and historically the Russian Empire.', 'Subdivided into 100 kopecks; one of the oldest currencies in continuous European use.'),
    ('RUPEE', 'South Asian Currency', 'Official monetary unit of India, Pakistan, Sri Lanka, Nepal, and Mauritius.', 'The Indian rupee uses the currency sign ₹; subdivided historically into paise.'),
    ('SAHARA', 'Vast Desert', 'The largest hot desert in the world, covering over 3.5 million square miles.', 'Features shifting sand ergs, rocky plateaus, and subterranean desert oases.'),
    ('SAMURAI', 'Hereditary Japanese Warrior', 'Hereditary military nobility and officer caste of medieval and early-modern Japan.', 'Followed the strict Bushido moral warrior code and carried twin katana and wakizashi swords.'),
    ('SANJOSE', 'Costa Rican Capital', 'Central valley capital of Costa Rica surrounded by cloud forests and volcanoes.', 'Home to the ornate neoclassical National Theatre of Costa Rica and the Pre-Columbian Gold Museum.'),
    ('SANTIAGO', 'Chilean Capital', 'Vibrant capital of Chile nestled in a central valley surrounded by towering snow Andes.', 'Features the historic Plaza de Armas and the towering Gran Torre Santiago skyscraper.'),
    ('SATURN', 'Ringed Giant', 'Sixth planet from the Sun celebrated for vast, brilliant icy rings.', 'Features dozens of moons including methane-rich Titan and Enceladus.'),
    ('SAVANNA', 'Tropical Grassland', 'Mixed woodland-grassland ecosystem characterized by widely spaced trees and dry seasons.', 'Covers vast expanses of East Africa, supporting massive seasonal wildlife migrations.'),
    ('SAXOPHONE', 'Single-Reed Woodwind', 'Woodwind musical instrument usually made of brass and played with a single-reed mouthpiece.', 'Invented by Belgian instrument maker Adolphe Sax in 1840; central to jazz music.'),
    ('SEA', 'Saline Ocean', 'Vast body of salt water covering more than seventy percent of Earth.', 'Encompasses interconnected oceans, seas, and gulfs globally.'),
    ('SEISMOLOGY', 'Earthquake Study', 'Scientific study of earthquakes, tectonic movements, and propagation of elastic waves.', 'Seismologists use sensitive seismographs to locate epicenters and predict tsunamis.'),
    ('SENATE', 'Governing Council', 'Deliberative assembly with political and legislative governing authority.', 'The Roman Senate debated foreign treaties, laws, and public spending.'),
    ('SEOUL', 'Dynamic Capital', 'High-tech metropolis and capital of South Korea situated along the Han River.', 'Blends Joseon dynasty royal palaces like Gyeongbokgung with cutting-edge tech.'),
    ('SHAKESPEARE', 'The Bard of Avon', 'English playwright, poet, and actor widely regarded as the greatest dramatist in history.', 'Penned timeless theatrical masterpieces including Hamlet, Macbeth, Romeo and Juliet, and Othello.'),
    ('SHEKEL', 'Israeli Currency', 'Official currency of the State of Israel, also used in the Palestinian territories.', 'Ancient biblical unit of weight revived as modern legal tender denominated as New Shekel.'),
    ('SHOGUN', 'Japanese Military Commander', 'Hereditary military dictator of Japan from 1192 until the Meiji Restoration in 1868.', 'Held de facto political and military power while the Emperor remained a symbolic figurehead.'),
    ('SILVER', 'Lustrous Metal', 'Precious metallic element with atomic number 47 and highest conductivity.', 'Historically minted into currency coins and used in fine silverware.'),
    ('SINGAPORE', 'Lion City', 'Prosperous sovereign island city-state in Southeast Asia renowned for futuristic gardens.', "Features Marina Bay Sands, Changi Airport's Jewel, and Gardens by the Bay."),
    ('SKIN', 'Body Covering', 'The largest organ of the human body, serving as a protective shield.', 'Regulates body temperature and houses sensory tactile touch receptors.'),
    ('SKY', 'Atmosphere Vault', 'The expanse of air over the Earth appearing blue during the daytime.', 'Scatters short blue light wavelengths through Rayleigh scattering.'),
    ('SOCRATES', 'Classical Philosopher', 'Foundational Greek philosopher of Athens renowned for the Socratic questioning method.', 'Sentenced to drink hemlock in 399 BC for corrupting youth and defying state gods.'),
    ('SODIUM', 'Alkali Metal', 'Soft, highly reactive silvery alkali metal with atomic number 11.', 'Combines with chlorine gas to form common dietary table salt crystals.'),
    ('SOLSTICE', 'Extreme Sun Position', 'Astronomical event when the Sun reaches its highest or lowest excursion relative to celestial equator.', 'The summer solstice marks the longest day of the year; the winter solstice marks the shortest.'),
    ('SONATA', 'Solo Composition', 'Musical composition for a solo instrument or small ensemble, usually in three or four movements.', 'Classical piano sonatas feature exposition, development, and recapitulation structural phases.'),
    ('SONG', 'Vocal Melody', 'Musical piece composed of lyrics sung by voices, often with instruments.', 'Conveys emotional feelings, storytelling, and cultural traditions.'),
    ('SOVEREIGNTY', 'Supreme Authority', 'Supreme power or authority of an independent nation to govern its own affairs.', 'Guarantees that independent nations control borders, laws, and foreign policy.'),
    ('SPHINX', 'Mythic Beast', "Mythological monster with a lion's body and human head posing riddles.", 'The Great Sphinx of Giza stands sentinel guard before the pyramids.'),
    ('STAR', 'Luminous Sphere', 'Luminous sphere of plasma held together by its own gravity in space.', 'Undergoes continuous nuclear fusion in its core.'),
    ('STATUE', 'Carved Figure', 'Three-dimensional carved or cast sculpture representing a person or animal.', 'The Statue of Liberty in New York Harbor greeted millions of immigrants.'),
    ('STEPPE', 'Temperate Grassland', 'Vast ecoregion of semiarid, unforested grass plains spanning across Eurasia.', 'Historically traversed by nomadic horse cultures including the Mongols and Scythians.'),
    ('STOCKHOLM', 'Venice of the North', 'Capital of Sweden built across an archipelago of fourteen picturesque islands.', 'Features the cobbled Old Town (Gamla Stan), royal palaces, and the 1628 Vasa ship museum.'),
    ('STONEHENGE', 'Standing Megaliths', 'Prehistoric megalithic monument consisting of a ring of standing stones in Wiltshire, England.', 'Aligned with the rising sun of the summer solstice and sunset of winter solstice.'),
    ('STRAIT', 'Narrow Sea Channel', 'Naturally formed, narrow waterway connecting two larger navigable bodies of water.', 'The Strait of Gibraltar connects the Atlantic Ocean to the Mediterranean Sea.'),
    ('STRATOSPHERE', 'Upper Atmosphere', "The second major layer of Earth's atmosphere situated above the troposphere.", 'Contains the protective ozone layer that filters out harmful solar ultraviolet radiation.'),
    ('SUEZ', 'Sea-Level Egyptian Canal', 'Artificial sea-level waterway in Egypt connecting the Mediterranean Sea to the Red Sea.', 'Opened in 1869; provides the shortest maritime shipping route between Europe and Asia.'),
    ('SUN', 'Central Star', 'The yellow dwarf star at the gravitational center of our Solar System.', 'Powers all life on Earth through light and heat.'),
    ('SUPERIOR', 'Largest Great Lake', 'The largest freshwater lake in the world by surface area, shared by the United States and Canada.', "The northernmost and westernmost of North America's five Great Lakes, holding immense water volume."),
    ('SUPERNOVA', 'Stellar Explosion', 'Powerful and luminous stellar explosion occurring during the last evolutionary stages of a star.', 'Can briefly outshine an entire galaxy of stars while scattering heavy elements into space.'),
    ('SUVA', 'Pacific Capital', 'Bustling capital and largest metropolitan city of the island nation of Fiji.', 'Major cultural and commercial hub of the South Pacific, situated on Viti Levu.'),
    ('SYMBIOSIS', 'Biological Partnership', 'Close and long-term biological interaction between two different biological species.', 'Mutualism benefits both species, like clownfish living protected among anemone tentacles.'),
    ('SYMPHONY', 'Orchestral Masterwork', 'Elaborate musical composition for full orchestra, typically in four distinct movements.', 'Pioneered by Haydn, Mozart, and Beethoven with majestic brass, woodwinds, and strings.'),
    ('TAHOE', 'Deep Alpine Lake', 'Large freshwater lake in the Sierra Nevada mountains straddling California and Nevada.', 'Renowned for crystal-clear cobalt blue waters and surrounding alpine ski peaks.'),
    ('TAIGA', 'Boreal Conifer Forest', "The world's largest land biome, consisting of vast subarctic coniferous pine forests.", 'Spans northern Russia, Scandinavia, and Canada, acting as a colossal carbon sink.'),
    ('TAJMAHAL', 'Marble Mausoleum', 'Ivory-white marble mausoleum on the Yamuna river in Agra, India.', 'Commissioned in 1632 by Mughal emperor Shah Jahan to house the tomb of his wife Mumtaz.'),
    ('TALE', 'Narrative Story', 'Story or narrative recounting events, adventures, or moral lessons.', 'Passed down through oral traditions and bedtime storytelling.'),
    ('TASMANIA', 'Australian Island State', 'Island state of Australia located 150 miles south of the mainland across Bass Strait.', 'Known for vast rugged wilderness national parks and the native carnivorous Tasmanian devil.'),
    ('TEGUCIGALPA', 'Honduran Capital', 'Mountainous capital city of Honduras situated in a high central valley.', 'Historic silver-mining colonial town with winding hillside streets and pine forests.'),
    ('TEHRAN', 'Persian Capital', 'Sprawling capital of Iran nestled beneath the dramatic snowy Alborz mountains.', 'Home to the opulent Golestan Palace complex and the National Jewels Museum.'),
    ('TEMPLE', 'Sacred Shrine', 'Building dedicated to religious ceremonies and the worship of deities.', 'Ancient Greek, Roman, and Hindu temples feature majestic stone columns.'),
    ('TESLA', 'Electrical Visionary', 'Serbian-American inventor and electrical engineer who pioneered alternating current (AC).', 'Invented the induction motor, Tesla coil, and envisioned wireless global electrical transmission.'),
    ('THAMES', 'London River', 'River flowing through southern England and the heart of downtown London into North Sea.', 'Historically froze solid in winter during the Little Ice Age, hosting festive frost fairs.'),
    ('THANKSGIVING', 'Harvest Gratitude Holiday', 'National holiday celebrated in the United States and Canada giving thanks for the harvest.', 'Traditionally celebrated with family feasts featuring roast turkey, stuffing, and pumpkin pie.'),
    ('THEORY', 'Scientific Model', 'Well-substantiated explanation of some aspect of the natural world.', 'Supported by vast bodies of empirical facts, testing, and laws.'),
    ('THERMODYNAMICS', 'Heat and Energy Laws', 'Branch of physics dealing with heat, work, entropy, and energy transformation.', 'Establishes that total energy is conserved and entropy continually increases.'),
    ('THOR', 'Norse God of Thunder', 'Hammer-wielding Norse god associated with thunder, lightning, storms, strength, and sacred protection.', 'Wielded the magical hammer Mjolnir, wore the strength belt Megingjord, and rode in a goat chariot.'),
    ('TIDE', 'Ocean Bulge', 'Periodic rising and falling of ocean sea levels caused by the Moon.', 'Tidal forces create high and low tides twice daily along coasts.'),
    ('TIME', 'Temporal Progress', 'Continuous progress of existence from the past through present to future.', 'Measured chronologically using solar cycles and atomic vibrations.'),
    ('TITAN', 'Atmospheric Moon', 'The largest moon of Saturn and only natural satellite known to have a dense atmosphere.', 'Features rivers, lakes, and seas of liquid methane and ethane across frozen ice bedrock.'),
    ('TOKYO', 'Vibrant Megacity', "High-tech capital of Japan and the world's most populous metropolitan area.", 'Blends neon skyscrapers, historic Shinto shrines, and world-class sushi dining.'),
